From f9a4af046688b576bdce448218dd2e7ecbe6b7d6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ANiri anland audio fix <anland-audio@localhost>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 01:09:19 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] backend/anland: close sender_fd on every sender-thread exit
 path

sender_thread() returned directly from the SEND_DEAD case:

    case SEND_DEAD:
        atomic_store_explicit(&a->stop_requested, true, memory_order_release);
        return NULL;

which skipped the trailing close(fd). Every SEND_DEAD outcome therefore leaked
sender_fd: EPIPE / ECONNRESET / ENOTCONN from sendmsg, a short write, and the
unknown-error branch. detach_audio_fd_locked() does not compensate -- with
sender_started set it only pthread_join()s and then sets sock_fd = -1, and the
loop thread's own close(sender_fd) is reserved for the case where
pthread_create() failed, so the descriptor was genuinely lost.

The function now has a single exit:

    case SEND_DEAD:
        atomic_store_explicit(&a->stop_requested, true, memory_order_release);
        goto out;
    ...
out:
    close(fd);
    return NULL;

so sender_fd is closed exactly once on every path this thread can take. The
ownership split is unchanged and now holds without exception: io_fd belongs to
the PipeWire io source, sender_fd belongs to the sender thread, and the loop
thread only closes sender_fd when the thread never started.

Also removed send_ring_used(), which has had no callers since the sender stopped
using it to clear the queue on detach (the detach path now moves tail up to head
directly). Verified with real code generation rather than -fsyntax-only, which
never reports -Wunused-function: the warning fires on f337d2d and is gone here.

No other change. wire framing, the sender architecture, playback_ready, the slot
epoch, the keep-alive and the mic threading are all untouched, and the
format-change window is still only described in the docs.
---
 src/backend/anland/c/anland_audio.c | 27 ++++++++++++++-------------
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/backend/anland/c/anland_audio.c b/src/backend/anland/c/anland_audio.c
index 4920ec8..668c21f 100644
--- a/src/backend/anland/c/anland_audio.c
+++ b/src/backend/anland/c/anland_audio.c
@@ -227,12 +227,6 @@ static bool send_ring_init(struct send_ring *r, size_t size)
     return true;
 }
 
-static size_t send_ring_used(const struct send_ring *r)
-{
-    return (size_t)(atomic_load_explicit(&r->head, memory_order_acquire) -
-                    atomic_load_explicit(&r->tail, memory_order_relaxed));
-}
-
 /* Producer. Copies one whole message plus its local slot header, or reports failure so the
  * caller can count a drop. Never splits a message and never blocks. `epoch` is the
  * attachment generation the caller observed for this period. */
@@ -483,13 +477,13 @@ static void *sender_thread(void *data)
         }
 
         case SEND_DEAD:
-            /* Raise the flag for the loop thread and return. Do NOT call sender_wake()
-             * here: that pipe is read by this very thread, so it cannot wake the loop.
-             * The loop thread picks stop_requested up on its 1 s periodic tick
-             * (service_rt_state) and performs the detach. The sender is already gone by
+            /* Raise the flag for the loop thread and leave through the common exit. Do NOT
+             * call sender_wake() here: that pipe is read by this very thread, so it cannot
+             * wake the loop -- the loop thread picks stop_requested up on its 1 s periodic
+             * tick (service_rt_state) and performs the detach. The sender is already gone by
              * then, which detach_audio_fd_locked() handles through sender_started. */
             atomic_store_explicit(&a->stop_requested, true, memory_order_release);
-            return NULL;
+            goto out;
 
         case SEND_EMPTY:
         default:
@@ -504,9 +498,16 @@ static void *sender_thread(void *data)
         }
     }
 
-    /* No flush on the way out: a detach is not a place to deliver one last period of audio
+out:
+    /* The single exit path for every way this thread can end -- normal stop or SEND_DEAD.
+     * No flush on the way out: a detach is not a place to deliver one last period of audio
      * to a consumer that is going away, and waiting for the kernel here would only extend
-     * the join. Whatever is still queued is dropped by the detach path. */
+     * the join. Whatever is still queued is dropped by the detach path.
+     *
+     * This is the ONLY place sender_fd is closed on the running-thread path, which is what
+     * makes "exactly one close" hold: detach_audio_fd_locked() only pthread_join()s when
+     * sender_started is set, and the loop thread's own close(sender_fd) is reserved for the
+     * pthread_create() failure case where this thread never came into existence. */
     close(fd);
     return NULL;
 }
-- 
